  message: "DONE across two PRs. PR #371: snapshot v2 (verdict + caveat kinds + credited-flows zero/nonzero bucket per claim; the INV-zuhig vacuousness shape — green verdict, dead evidence — now fails the gate), comparison logic extracted to scripts/check-self-claims-drift with 13 logic tests, snapshot re-recorded from the merged post-#367 tree (18/18 confirmed_with_caveats, 4 claims crediting nonzero; the committed snapshot had said 18x inconclusive since pre-climb, so the next cron would have failed on the improvement), generate-security-md v2-aware with two stale-FALSE prose paragraphs corrected. Follow-up PR (dev 097ab4e05a): probing the merged PR revealed the per-PR arm was wired into GHA ci.yml while the CI that gates merges is Woodpecker (auto-pr polls only ci/woodpecker/pr/woodpecker), AND the live Woodpecker full-suite cron had dropped check-self-claims at cutover — the gate SECURITY.md names had been running NOWHERE. Both arms now live in the Woodpecker pipelines: per-PR path-filtered on the claim surface in the gating context, unconditional on the cron for analyzer-change drift. Validation caveat, stated rather than hidden: the follow-up PR's own diff does not match the gate's path filter, so the per-PR step has not yet had a live run — first exercises are tonight's 01:00 UTC cron (unconditional arm) and the next claim-surface PR (INV-titih is likely). If the step has an install-level defect the cron surfaces it within a cycle."  # 8641
